  "description": "Son Heung-min left home at 16, and in 2025 LAFC paid a reported fee of up to 26.5 million dollars, an MLS record.\n\nSources:\n- Wikipedia: Son Heung-min: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Son_Heung-min\n- MLSsoccer.com: LAFC set MLS transfer record with Son Heung-Min signing: https://www.mlssoccer.com/news/lafc-break-mls-transfer-record-son-heung-min-signing-tottenham-south-korea\n\nFrom the cited pages: in August 2008 Son joined Hamburger SV's youth academy at 16; on 28 August 2015 he joined Tottenham for 22 million pounds, the most expensive Asian player in football history at the time; in 2021-22 he won the Premier League Golden Boot with 23 goals, shared with Mohamed Salah, the first Asian player to do so; on 6 August 2025 he joined LAFC after 10 years at Tottenham, for a reported fee of up to 26.5 million dollars, an MLS record; the previous record was a reported 22 million dollars plus add-ons (Atlanta United, Emmanuel Latte Lath). Fees are reported, not officially confirmed. Not financial advice.\n\n#shorts #sonheungmin #lafc #howtheymakemoney",
